    "text": "ladailypost.com\nwebsite\nDeming\nNew Mexico State Ethics Commission Announces Settlements With Deming City Officials For Governmental Conduct Act Violations\nBy Submitted by,\n22 hours agoALBUQUERQUE — The New Mexico State Ethics Commission has reached settlement agreements with Deming City Councilors Irma Rodriguez and Joe “Butter” Milo, with related compliance obligations involving Deming City Manager Aaron Sera, resolving alleged violations of the Governmental Conduct Act. The Commission alleged that Councilor Rodriguez failed...\n1\nComments\nYOU MAY ALSO LIKE\nThe KLC Journal\n·\nuser · 687 followers\nDavid Heitz\n·\nuser · 29.8K followers\nThree Denver council members put homeless family in hotel, cop buys unhoused man breakfast\nDenver City Council members Serena Gonzales Guttierez, Sarah Parady and Shontel Lewis combined forces after Monday’s meeting and helped a family that had been told no shelter was available, Housekeys Action Network Denver posted Tuesday on social media.\nDenver, CO ·22d",
